robots sent from the future to protect  us the plot of Terminator 2 may be  science fiction but thanks to engineers  at Boston Dynamics the idea may not be  as far-fetched as we think come with me  if you want to live  this is PETMAN an anthropomorphic robot  designed to test the kind of search and  rescue clothing used during reactor  meltdowns or worse nuclear war the  company debuted an early version of  Catman in 2011 seen here going for a  stroll and knocking out some push-ups  almost two years later pet man still  enjoys walking on the treadmill but the  latest version has undergone a  significant evolution he now perfectly  emulates a human beings full range of  motion essential to testing clothing  made to withstand exposure to hazardous  chemicals it's just the latest  experiment in the company's line of  lifelike military innovations  you may remember cheetah a DARPA  commissioned robot that set a land speed  record of nearly 30 miles per hour  setting off military dreams of an ultra  fast companion for foot soldiers then  there was Big Dawg also a DARPA project  which Boston Dynamics set free to roam  the beaches of Thailand in a display of  its ability to carry heavy cargo across  tricky terrain as for pet man the  Pentagon reportedly hopes to use the  robot for more than just testing hazmat  suits it could be sent in on solo rescue  missions in the event of a biological  attack  you
 

